      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Having the hip and feet set to Animate will fix this, but not ideal if your animation is not setup exactly to have head at the same place as the view point. It will result in stretch neck or hunch.\nSomething to note, the transition is smoother if everything stay tracking from the start. Having Animation in between will create a snap. But with IK 2.0 the drag feet happen when having that setup.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
